== Where to Buy ==
* [[Arrow Crafting]] is a highly effective method of gaining different kinds of arrows not easily found. This skill can only be obtained by a [[Archer Skill Quest|quest]].
* The [[Ore Downgrading]] quest and [[Sorcerer]]'s [[Element Analyze]] skill can be used to get materials for elemental arrows.
* {{item |id=1752 Fire Arrows}} can be bought from the following [[NPC]]s:
** {{shop |id=albtrea_tool Alberta Island Tool Dealer}}
** {{shop |id=ein_tool Einbech Tool Dealer}}
** {{shop |id=lhz_arrow Lighthalzen Arrow Dealer}}
* {{item |id=1751 Silver Arrows}} can be bought from the same [[NPC]]s for {{item |id=1752 Fire Arrows}}, plus the following [[NPC]]s:
** {{shop |id=alb_weapon1 Alberta Weapon Dealer 1}}
** {{shop |id=arch_tool Archer Village Tool Dealer}}
** {{shop |id=gef_weapon1 Geffen Weapon Dealer 1}}
** {{shop |id=iz_weapon Izlude Weapon Dealer}}
** {{shop |id=yuno_weapon Juno Weapon Dealer}}
** {{shop |id=moc_weapon1 Morroc Weapon Dealer 1}}
** {{shop |id=pay_weapon1 Payon Weapon Dealer 1}}
** {{shop |id=prt_weapon1 Prontera Weapon Dealer 1}}
* {{item|id=1773 Elven Arrows}} and {{item|id=1774 Hunting Arrows}} can be bought from the {{shop |id=mora_tool Mora Village Tool Dealer}}
* One of the rarest arrows, {{item |id=12183 Immaterial Arrow}} are ineffective against [[Neutral]] property monsters, but are highly effective against [[Ghost]] property monsters. The easiest method of obtaining them is by crafting from an {{item |id=714 Emperium}}, a {{item |id=7108 Piece of Shield}}, or a {{item |id=7450 Skeletal Armor Piece}}.
* The rarest arrow regularly used is the {{item |id=1772 Holy Arrow}}. It can be obtained from {{item |id=12183 Holy Arrow Quivers}}, which are dropped by two monsters at the [[Rachel Sanctuary]], or crafting from {{item |id=7435 Golden Ornaments}} and {{item |id=7510 Valhalla's Flowers}}, which are dropped by {{monster |id=1700 Dame of Sentinel}} and by {{monster |id=1765 Valkyries}}, respectively. It is superior to the {{item |id=1751 Silver Arrow}}.
* It is possible to stack 500 arrows in a quiver and lower their weight through an [[NPC]] called ''Inventor Jaax'', in the weapon shop of [[Payon]]. It is usually better weight-wise to simply craft them. However, it is possible to open a quiver while being overweight, when [[Arrow Crafting]] is disabled. Quivers are also good for arrows bought from [[NPC]]s.
* Remember to un-equip any arrows that you currently have equipped if you plan to make a quiver of said arrow type. For example, say you currently have 700 {{item |id=1750 Arrows}} equipped and you want to make a quiver with them and keep the remaining 200 equipped. You need to un-equip them first before he can make a quiver for you.

