[[Category: Item Mixing]]

Scrolls are special consumable items that enable the user to cast a spell that may not normally be available to them, without spending [[SP]].
When using a spell via a scroll, all calculations are handled as if you're actually casting the spell yourself: MATK, casting time and so on, and are influenced by your equipment.

== List ==
* [[Fire_Ball|Fire Ball]] {{Item|id=696 Level 1}}
* [[Fire_Wall|Fire Wall]] {{Item|id=698 Level 1}}, {{Item|id=699 Level 5}}
* [[Frost_Diver|Frost Diver]] {{Item|id=700 Level 1}}
* [[Teleport]] {{Item|id=12003 Level 1}}
* [[Cold_Bolt|Cold Bolt]] {{Item|id=688 Level 3}}, {{Item|id=689 Level 5}}
* [[Earth_Spike|Earth Spike]] {{Item|id=686 Level 3}}, {{Item|id=687 Level 5}}
* [[Fire_Bolt|Bolt]] {{Item|id=690 Level 3}}, {{Item|id=691 Level 5}}
* [[Heal]] {{Item|id=12001 Level 3}}, {{Item|id=12002 Level 5}}
* [[Lightning_Bolt|Lightning Bolt]] {{Item|id=692 Level 3}}, {{Item|id=693 Level 5}}
* [[Soul_Strike|Soul Strike]] {{Item|id=694 Level 3}}, {{Item|id=695 Level 5}}

== Special exception ==
Although usually scrolls are expended when used, there is an exception: a [[TaeKwon_Kid|Taekwon]]-class character in [[TaeKwon_Kid#Happiness status|Happiness]] status can lower the chance of an [[Earth_Spike|Earth Spike]] (Either level 3 or 5) scroll actually burning up to as low as 1% per use by raising his or her [[Happy_Break|Happy Break]] skill. However, using a scroll in such way expends 10 [[SP]].
*Additional note: the scroll is consumed when you use it, not when you actually select a target and use the spell. Don't mash your activation hotkey.

